{
  "assessment": "The source provides a complete numerical study of spontaneous quantum turbulence in a 2D BEC via the Kibble-Zurek mechanism, with quantitative controls (quench time, temperature), readouts (vortex number, equilibration time, energy spectra, structure functions), and fitted power-law parameters. The evidence supports authoring an interactive experiment.",
  "status": "authored",
  "drafts": [
    {
      "design_summary": "Players quench a 2D BEC across the condensation transition and measure the vortex number and equilibration time as functions of quench time. The historical world follows Kibble-Zurek scaling with a power-law exponent near -1/2 for vortex number and +1/2 for equilibration time. The counterfactual world selects a different reported regime where the compressible energy scaling changes dramatically with temperature, but for the chosen readouts (vortex number and equilibration time) the counterfactual uses the same KZ mechanism. To create a meaningful relationship-level difference, the counterfactual world instead uses the reported high-temperature regime where compressible energy is nearly independent of quench time, but that requires a different readout. Since the card does not report an alternative regime for vortex number or equilibration time, we select the reported regime selection between low-temperature and high-temperature compressible energy scaling, using total_compressible_energy as the readout. The historical world uses the low-temperature scaling E_c ~ tau_Q^{-0.902}, while the counterfactual uses the high-temperature scaling E_c ~ tau_Q^{-0.019}. This yields a clear difference in direction (decreasing vs approximately invariant) under the same controls (quench_time, temperature).",
      "information_boundary": {
        "shared_player": {
          "items": [
            "The system is a 2D homogeneous Bose-Einstein condensate in a periodic box, quenched through the condensation transition by linearly ramping the chemical potential.",
            "The quench time tau_Q is a control variable ranging from 10 to 1000 (dimensionless).",
            "The temperature T is a control variable ranging from 1e-6 to 1 (dimensionless), with T=1 corresponding to O(1) nK.",
            "The vortex number and total compressible energy are measured at the equilibration time, which is defined as the time when the growth of boson number changes from exponential to linear.",
            "Simulations are averaged over many realizations (e.g., R=1000 or R=2000) and reported with 1 standard deviation error bars.",
            "The system is in the low-temperature limit (of order 1 nK or less) to isolate spontaneous quantum turbulence from BKT effects.",
            "Mean-field critical exponents nu=1/2 and z=2 are used."
          ],
          "claim_ids": [
            "vortex_number_kz_scaling",
            "equilibration_time_scaling",
            "compressible_energy_scaling_T1",
            "compressible_energy_scaling_Tlow"
          ],
          "mechanism_ids": [
            "kibble_zurek_vortex_formation",
            "compressible_energy_scaling"
          ],
          "line_ranges": [
            {"line_start": 108, "line_end": 113},
            {"line_start": 142, "line_end": 142},
            {"line_start": 365, "line_end": 365},
            {"line_start": 466, "line_end": 466},
            {"line_start": 477, "line_end": 480},
            {"line_start": 606, "line_end": 613}
          ]
        },
        "identification_only": {
          "items": [
            "The vortex number follows a power-law in quench time: n_v = A * tau_Q^exponent, with a fitted exponent near -1/2.",
            "The equilibration time follows a power-law in quench time: t_eq = A * tau_Q^exponent, with a fitted exponent near +1/2.",
            "The total compressible energy follows a power-law in quench time: E_c = A * tau_Q^exponent, with an exponent that depends on temperature.",
            "At low temperature (T=1e-6), the compressible energy exponent is near -1, while at high temperature (T=1) it is near 0.",
            "The system exhibits universal scaling of energy spectra under Kibble-Zurek rescaling."
          ],
          "claim_ids": [
            "vortex_number_kz_scaling",
            "equilibration_time_scaling",
            "compressible_energy_scaling_T1",
            "compressible_energy_scaling_Tlow"
          ],
          "mechanism_ids": [
            "kibble_zurek_vortex_formation",
            "compressible_energy_scaling"
          ],
          "line_ranges": [
            {"line_start": 158, "line_end": 163},
            {"line_start": 612, "line_end": 613},
            {"line_start": 662, "line_end": 663}
          ]
        },
        "oracle_only": {
          "items": [
            "The exact fitted amplitude and exponent values for the vortex number scaling: n_v = 249.036 * tau_Q^{-0.534}.",
            "The exact fitted amplitude and exponent values for the equilibration time scaling: t_eq = 3.779 * tau_Q^{0.541} + 0.078 * tau_Q.",
            "The exact fitted amplitude and exponent values for the compressible energy at T=1: E_c = 3977.0 * tau_Q^{-0.019}.",
            "The exact fitted amplitude and exponent values for the compressible energy at T=1e-6: E_c = 7422.0 * tau_Q^{-0.902}.",
            "The exact form of the universal collapse: E_i(k) tau_Q^{3/4} = F(k tau_Q^{1/4})."
          ],
          "claim_ids": [
            "vortex_number_kz_scaling",
            "equilibration_time_scaling",
            "compressible_energy_scaling_T1",
            "compressible_energy_scaling_Tlow"
          ],
          "mechanism_ids": [
            "kibble_zurek_vortex_formation",
            "compressible_energy_scaling"
          ],
          "line_ranges": [
            {"line_start": 161, "line_end": 163},
            {"line_start": 496, "line_end": 497},
            {"line_start": 612, "line_end": 612},
            {"line_start": 662, "line_end": 662}
          ]
        }
      },
      "counterfactual_derivation": {
        "kind": "reported_regime_selection",
        "description": "The counterfactual world selects the high-temperature regime (T=1) for the compressible energy scaling, as reported in the paper, instead of the low-temperature regime (T=1e-6). The paper reports two distinct power-law behaviors for the total compressible energy as a function of quench time: at T=1, E_c ~ tau_Q^{-0.019} (nearly independent), and at T=1e-6, E_c ~ tau_Q^{-0.902} (strongly decreasing). The selector parameter chooses between these two reported branches.",
        "source_claim_ids": [
          "compressible_energy_scaling_T1",
          "compressible_energy_scaling_Tlow"
        ],
        "source_mechanism_ids": [
          "compressible_energy_scaling"
        ],
        "selector_parameter": "temperature_regime_selector",
        "historical_value": 0,
        "counterfactual_value": 1,
        "paper_defined_equations_unchanged": true
      },
      "relationship_targets": [
        {
          "control": "quench_time",
          "readout": "total_compressible_energy",
          "historical_direction": "decreasing",
          "counterfactual_direction": "approximately_invariant",
          "historical_shape": "power-law decay with exponent -0.902",
          "counterfactual_shape": "power-law with exponent -0.019, nearly flat",
          "source_claim_ids": [
            "compressible_energy_scaling_T1",
            "compressible_energy_scaling_Tlow"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "candidate": {
        "family": "kibble_zurek_turbulence",
        "title": "Compressible Energy Scaling in a Quenched 2D BEC",
        "claim": "The total compressible kinetic energy at equilibration time scales as a power law in quench time, with an exponent that depends strongly on temperature: at low temperature (T=1e-6) it decreases as tau_Q^{-0.902}, while at high temperature (T=1) it is nearly independent of tau_Q with exponent -0.019.",
        "source": {
          "citation": "Seong-Ho Shinn et al., Spontaneous Quantum Turbulence in a Newborn Bose-Einstein Condensate via the Kibble-Zurek Mechanism, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/b16v-hwp2",
          "journal_doi": "10.1103/b16v-hwp2",
          "arxiv_versioned_id": "2506.21670v3",
          "locator": "Lines 612-613 and 662-663",
          "role": "source"
        },
        "apparatus": {
          "name": "quenched_bec_simulator",
          "description": "A numerical simulator of a 2D homogeneous Bose-Einstein condensate in a periodic box, quenched through the condensation transition by linearly ramping the chemical potential. The simulator solves the stochastic projected Gross-Pitaevskii equation and reports ensemble-averaged observables at the equilibration time."
        },
        "background": "When a 2D Bose-Einstein condensate is quenched through the condensation transition, the Kibble-Zurek mechanism predicts the formation of topological defects (vortices). The resulting turbulent state exhibits scaling laws for vortex number, equilibration time, and kinetic energy spectra. The compressible kinetic energy, associated with sound waves, shows a temperature-dependent scaling with quench time.",
        "initial_observations": [
          "The system exhibits a turbulent state with vortices after the quench.",
          "The total compressible kinetic energy can be measured at the equilibration time.",
          "The compressible energy depends on the quench time and the temperature."
        ],
        "controls": [
          {
            "name": "quench_time",
            "description": "Duration of the linear quench of the chemical potential from mu_i to mu_f.",
            "unit": "dimensionless",
            "minimum": 10,
            "maximum": 1000
          },
          {
            "name": "temperature",
            "description": "Temperature in dimensionless units, with T=1 corresponding to O(1) nK.",
            "unit": "dimensionless",
            "minimum": 1e-06,
            "maximum": 1
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "name": "total_compressible_energy",
            "description": "Total compressible kinetic energy at equilibration time, integrated over all wavenumbers.",
            "unit": "dimensionless",
            "resolution": 0.1
          }
        ],
        "oracle": {
          "kind": "closed_form",
          "outputs": {
            "total_compressible_energy": {
              "op": "multiply",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "add",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "multiply",
                      "args": [
                        {"var": "temperature_regime_selector"},
                        {"param": "compressible_energy_amplitude_T1"}
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "multiply",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "subtract",
                          "args": [
                            {"var": "one"},
                            {"var": "temperature_regime_selector"}
                          ]
                        },
                        {"param": "compressible_energy_amplitude_Tlow"}
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "power",
                  "args": [
                    {"var": "quench_time"},
                    {
                      "op": "add",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "multiply",
                          "args": [
                            {"var": "temperature_regime_selector"},
                            {"param": "compressible_energy_exponent_T1"}
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "multiply",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "subtract",
                              "args": [
                                {"var": "one"},
                                {"var": "temperature_regime_selector"}
                              ]
                            },
                            {"param": "compressible_energy_exponent_Tlow"}
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "paper_parameters": {
            "compressible_energy_amplitude_T1": 3977.0,
            "compressible_energy_exponent_T1": -0.019,
            "compressible_energy_amplitude_Tlow": 7422.0,
            "compressible_energy_exponent_Tlow": -0.902
          },
          "counterfactual_parameters": {
            "compressible_energy_amplitude_T1": 3977.0,
            "compressible_energy_exponent_T1": -0.019,
            "compressible_energy_amplitude_Tlow": 7422.0,
            "compressible_energy_exponent_Tlow": -0.902
          }
        },
        "diagnostic_conditions": [
          {
            "quench_time": 100,
            "temperature": 1e-06
          },
          {
            "quench_time": 100,
            "temperature": 1
          },
          {
            "quench_time": 500,
            "temperature": 1e-06
          },
          {
            "quench_time": 500,
            "temperature": 1
          }
        ],
        "hidden_conditions": [
          {
            "quench_time": 200,
            "temperature": 1e-06
          },
          {
            "quench_time": 200,
            "temperature": 1
          },
          {
            "quench_time": 800,
            "temperature": 1e-06
          },
          {
            "quench_time": 800,
            "temperature": 1
          }
        ],
        "budget": 20,
        "max_replicates": 1,
        "confidence_threshold": 0.95,
        "relative_tolerance": 0.1,
        "notes": [
          "The counterfactual world uses the high-temperature branch (T=1) for compressible energy scaling, while the historical world uses the low-temperature branch (T=1e-6).",
          "The selector parameter 'temperature_regime_selector' is set to 0 for historical and 1 for counterfactual.",
          "All other parameters are identical between worlds.",
          "The readout is the total compressible energy, which shows a clear difference in direction: decreasing vs approximately invariant.",
          "The diagnostic conditions are chosen to be within the source-supported domain and to distinguish the two regimes."
        ],
        "counterfactual_change": "The temperature regime is switched from low (T=1e-6) to high (T=1), changing the compressible energy scaling from a strong power-law decay to a nearly flat dependence on quench time."
      }
    }
  ]
}
